## Rules

- Every `quote` field MUST be an exact substring of the chunk referenced by its `chunk_id`. The verifier checks this mechanically — fabricated quotes are rejected.
- `char_start` is the 0-based character offset where the quote begins in the chunk. If you're unsure of the exact offset, provide your best estimate — the verifier uses substring matching, not offset matching, so an approximate offset is acceptable as long as the quote is an exact substring.
- If a section has no evidence in any chunk, emit `"verdict": "neutral"` with an empty `evidence` array. A neutral verdict with no evidence is honest; a verdict with a fabricated quote is not.
- No verdict or forecast input may be derived from `ignored_short_term` entries.

